The CLI turns engine results into stable human and machine contracts without hiding unresolved work.

# rule VerdictFirst

Write the decisive stderr line before details. stdout contains knowledge, artifacts, or structured rows only; diagnostics always carry the `hint:` prefix.

# invariant NonInteractive

Only project configuration may prompt, and only when stdin is a TTY. Every other command must finish unattended; spawned git commands disable credential prompts.

# rule NonEmptySuccess

A command that operated on no resolved subject exits 2 and explains the fix. Successful inherited context is not empty: it remains exit 0 and names its source on stderr.

# decision Layers

Command classes orchestrate one operation, `report.ts` owns shared verdict and exit semantics, and terminal concerns stay at the CLI edge. Keep engine behavior out of Commander actions.

# decision AbsoluteContextPaths

For a plain context read, an absolute path explicitly selects the HINT project that contains it, independent of the caller's current working directory. Relative paths remain anchored to the current working directory so existing scripts keep their meaning.

# rule KnowledgeProfile

`repo: knowledge` suppresses code-target staleness and pending noise and enriches missing-path verdicts with local search suggestions. It must not alter stdout knowledge or turn a missing path into success.
